dash='## Quant & Market Dashboard\n\n### Liquidity and volatility\n\n- **Overnight:** The futures snapshot indicates technology-led gains, not order-book health. Current ES/NQ spreads, depth, overnight volume, ETF NBBO and Treasury depth are unverified. Refresh the execution feed; no reliable current liquidity rating is assigned.\n- **Holiday conditions:** SIFMA recommends a full fixed-income market close today for Veterans Day; firm decisions can differ. NYSE’s calendar does not list today as an equity holiday. Infer greater cross-asset execution caution, not a measured deterioration in depth. [SIFMA](https://www.sifma.org/news/press-releases/sifma-fixed-income-market-close-recommendation-in-the-u-s-the-u-k-and-japan-for-the-u-s-veterans-day-holiday-2026) · [NYSE](https://www.nyse.com/trade/hours-calendars).\n- **Funding:** Latest verified SOFR is 3.88% for November 9, updated November 10 at 07:02 CST; next FRED update is November 12. This lagged fixing does not diagnose current stress. [FRED](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/SOFR).\n- **Regime: Moderate; medium confidence.** Delayed VIX was 18.60 at November 11 06:36 EST / 05:36 CST, versus November 10 close 19.46. House bands: below 15 low, 15–25 moderate, 25–35 high, above 35 stressed; descriptive, not calibrated forecasts. Skew, term structure and dealer gamma are unverified. [VIX](https://chartexchange.com/symbol/index-vix/historical/).\n\n### Factor proxies\n\n| Factor | ETF | Nov 9→10 | Oct 9→Nov 10 (~1 month) |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Momentum | [MTUM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/mtum/history/) | -0.21% | -16.59% |\n| Value | [VLUE](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/vlue/history/) | -0.14% | -6.33% |\n| Quality | [QUAL](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/qual/history/) | -0.34% | -1.64% |\n| Size | [IWM](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwm/history/) | -0.68% | +0.59% |\n| Growth | [IWF](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/iwf/history/) | -0.86% | -10.86% |\n| Low volatility | [SPLV](https://stockanalysis.com/etf/splv/history/) | +0.33% | +8.25% |\n\nSource-linked split-adjusted Close-column price returns, excluding distributions, through November 10 at 16:00 EST / 15:00 CST. October 9 baselines are archived from the prior edition; latest closes were rechecked today. These are imperfect ETF proxies, not isolated factor premia. Corporate actions were not independently validated. Low volatility rose Tuesday while the other five fell; momentum and growth remain negative over the longer window.\n\n### Execution and microstructure\n\n- Cash opening auction: 08:30 CST / 14:30 UTC today. Yesterday’s CPI has been released; do not retain a pre-release event flag. Recheck exchange and product-specific holiday trading and settlement calendars.\n- SPY/QQQ: inspect quote age, NBBO spreads, depth, auction imbalances and ES/NQ basis. Use bounded limits and participation caps; stress slippage, gaps, cancellations, missed fills and latency. A technology-led rebound on thin depth can trap marketable orders.\n- Options: verify same-day expiry availability, deliverables and settlement. Reject stale, crossed or one-sided quotes. Near-expiry gamma can amplify hedging; dealer-gamma sign, expiry concentrations, pinning and flow magnitude remain unknown. Holiday-thinned underlying hedges are a scenario to test, not an observed fact.\n\n**Research watchlist:** SPY, QQQ, IWM, RSP, TLT; ES, NQ, ZN, VX; MTUM, VLUE, QUAL, IWF, SPLV; CRWV, NVDA, GOOGL.\n\n### DRL Improvements for the MATLAB System\n\n1. Enforce drawdown, exposure, participation and stale-data limits outside the policy, with an explicit safe fallback.\n2. Penalize spread, impact, turnover, latency and missed fills; stress permanent as well as transient impact and evaluate tail losses separately.\n3. Use purged walk-forward evaluation with training-only preprocessing and a one-use final holdout; separate holiday, event and ordinary sessions.\n4. Randomize depth and observation delays across regimes; test abstention when liquidity estimates or impact models are unreliable.\n\n### Model hygiene\n\nAudit leakage, survivorship bias, look-ahead, corporate actions, stale options quotes, multiple testing, calibration and drift. Preserve point-in-time universes, release vintages, missing-data flags and availability timestamps. Fit preprocessing inside training folds. An estimated impact-decay kernel is not itself causal identification.\n\n### MATLAB optimization patterns\n\n- Use named-zone timetables with exchange-specific calendars and causal synchronization.\n- Vectorize rolling features, preallocate logs and profile bottlenecks.\n- Parallelize independent folds or Bayesian trials with reproducible random streams and fixed budgets.\n- Use GPUs for sufficiently large batches; keep impact models, risk limits and evaluation modular.\n\n### High-value quant research question\n\n**Does an execution policy retain its net advantage when a fitted transient-impact model is replaced by a permanent-impact null at matched volatility and order-flow persistence?**\n\nUse matched seeds, risk budgets and fill assumptions in walk-forward tests. This tests whether apparent policy skill depends on an unidentified liquidity-recovery mechanism.\n'
